On Sun, 19 Jun 2005, Lara wrote:

> My main issues here are:
> 1) How do I get rid of my "burdened" state? I blessed my BoH (twice!), my
> Valkyrie is not so wimpy and I think I'm not carrying anything totally
> useless. I'm puzzled...

Put everything you don't use (ie all but armor, weapon, amulet, ring,
unihorn (plus magic whistle if you use pet)) in the BoH. And drop
everything you won't need in hell in a stash somewhere up (eg a chest at
DL1). Gems, not-combat wands (create monster, make inv, speed,...),
non-usefull rings,...) You don't need to carry everything.

> 2) Is my weaponry good enough to take on the critters down below?
> Should I get back to my stashes and resume Trollsbane, Ogresmasher and
> Cleaver? I feel really good with mojo and my faithful Vorpal Blade, but I
> don't know what to expect really.

Use Mojo (bless it first). And try twoweaponing with a silver saber
(minetown guard captazin should carry one, or maybe in Ludios). Demons and
Vampires *hate* silver. And enchant all that up to the top (+6/+7).

> 3) Is it safe to drink those 2 potions of gain level?

Yes, but you have better use for them. First of all, the lower your level,
the weaker the monsters generated. So keep your level as low as possible
unless you really need som skill slots (with a Valkyrie, you shouldn't).
If you can manage to curse your potions, they will make a fine escape way
once you'll carry the amulet (before that, the Orb provide levelport).
[eg to avoid crossing back painfull levels such as the Valley or Medusa
while going up with all the dungeon chasing after you (which is the best
thing that may happen to you soon, of course)]

Or you can give them (uncursed) to a pet able to drink them (if you're in
a mood to wish for a blessed figurine of an archon).

If you need to raise your HPs, alchemise potions of full healing.

> 4) I'm well aware I need to make my armor a bit better, but I'd have to make
> the scrolls myself... Is is worth it?

Yes. Fooproof your armor and enchant it to the top. Be sure your strength
is 25 with the GoP on, so you'll be able to throw Mojo (get shock
resistance before doing that). Oh, by the way, try to get the resistance
you're lacking. Being crowned is a good way for that.

> 5) How much should I donate to the priests to get clairvoyance? (money isn't
> an issue to me since I have all Ludios cleaned up and ready for looting)

200*XL. But that don't last long. Finding a magic lamp will be better for
permanent light source. Or wish for the eyes of the overworld. If you get
them, they'll be more than nice too.

Get speed boots. Wish for them if you don't manage to find one in the
Castle's armory or to polypile one.

Again, top-enchant all your armor and weapons.

Carry a second bag (not BoH) with one or two holy water and blessed scroll
of remove curse. If everything (including your BoH) get cursed in hell,
you'll appreciate.

